    "institutions_today": [],
    "paragraph": "A study using fine-grained human mobility data from four US metropolitan areas simulated the long-term impact of location-based recommender systems on food venue visitation and experienced income segregation under distance and capacity constraints. A multimodal diffusion framework synthesized streetscapes conditioned on explicit visual target proportions, text prompts, segmentation maps, and road masks using street-view imagery from Chicago and Orlando. Researchers analyzed bus mobility in Niterói, Brazil, using the NetMob 2026 dataset to examine passenger boarding patterns across urban zones, operational bottlenecks via vehicle GPS telemetry, and continuous trip duration predictions using supervised learning.",
